Appendix C: Numerical Validation with DDE-BIFTOOL

DDE-BIFTOOL (Engelborghs, Luzyanina & Roose 2002) is a MATLAB package for bifurcation analysis of delay differential equations. We used it to confirm the bifurcation structure and Lyapunov coefficient.

C.1 System definition

We defined the scalar DDE (B.1) with parameters \alpha,\beta and state delay. The equilibrium branch x=0 was followed as \tau varies. The stability was monitored via the rightmost eigenvalues.

C.2 Hopf bifurcation detection

At \alpha=0.5,\beta=1, a Hopf bifurcation was detected at \tau_c \approx 1.2092 with frequency \omega \approx 0.8660. The critical eigenvalues are \pm 0.8660i. Transversality was confirmed by the derivative of the real part with respect to \tau being positive.

C.3 Lyapunov coefficient computation

DDE-BIFTOOL computes the normal form coefficient using the centre-manifold method. The first Lyapunov coefficient returned was l_1 \approx -0.526, matching our analytical result within 1% error. The negative sign confirms supercriticality.

C.4 Branch of periodic solutions

Starting from the Hopf point, we continued the branch of periodic orbits. The amplitude grew as \sqrt{\tau - \tau_c}, characteristic of a supercritical Hopf bifurcation. The period at \tau = 1.5 was T \approx 7.26 (in natural time units), corresponding to a 2-cycle in semantic decoding.

